# Claude Code ready-for-review verification-cache opt-in.
#
# Presence of this file on the default branch (read from origin, never the
# working tree) lets ready-for-review's step 2 skip re-running this repo's
# test, lint, and typecheck commands when the same tree already passed them
# inside the freshness window.
#
# Committing it attests two things no tooling here can verify:
# 1. The default branch requires CI to pass before merge.
# 2. That CI runs the checks step 2 would otherwise run locally.
#
# Forks and copies: this attestation belongs to the repo that committed it.
# Delete it unless both facts hold for yours.
# To disable, delete this file from the default branch; existing worktrees
# keep the old state until their next git fetch.
# See docs/design-decisions/ready-for-review-verification-cache.md.
